* PieceSpice Tier-4 ideal-switch model for csd16412q5a
* Method: standard SPICE ideal voltage-controlled switch + offline LUT
* Losses handled offline in thermal post-processing (cf. PLECS P-TC).
* Standard SPICE SW primitive; no PLECS/SIMPLIS step-count or speed
* behavior is claimed for this emitted model.
* waveform_gate: retired_by_design
* Retired observables: dv/dt [INFERENCE], Miller droop (P-DEMO Fig. 6),
*   ringing [INFERENCE], reverse recovery (P-DEMO Fig. 7), voltage-
*   dependent capacitances, body-diode switching waveform.  dv/dt and
*   ringing are inferred from instantaneous switching and absent
*   parasitics; P-DEMO names the transient, Miller droop and recovery.
* These do not exist in this ideal-switch tier's electrical solution;
* energy/efficiency vs golden is scored offline, not on a converter bench.
* One measured LINEAR C_QOSS (Curve-4 Coss at cap_ref_Vds) is active only
* as a solver stabilizer: it slows drain dv/dt and adds L-C overshoot, so
* the DPT waveform gate stays retired_by_design.  It only prevents
* singular / no-capacitance solver steps; it is NOT a voltage-dependent
* or waveform-fidelity capacitance model.  Voltage-dependent capacitors
* and the body diode remain retired (see above).

.SUBCKT csd16412q5a_PIECESPICE_T4 d g s
* Pins: d=drain g=gate s=source (positional; gate threshold Vgs=V(g,s))

* --- ideal conduction (Curve-3 rds_on, measured Roff, Curve-7 Vth) ---
* temperature_c = 25 (config conditions.temperature)
* data_limitation: E_on/E_off and r_on are measured only at this
*   conditions.temperature = 25 C; the LUT has no temperature
*   axis and is valid only there.  It is a measured data slice, not a
*   physical guarantee at other junction temperatures.
*   The current 1x1 grid has 1 finite measured node(s) (capability 'constant_node'); no 2x2 interpolation cell has all four corners finite, so off-node queries are NaN / insufficient_measured_nodes and no bilinear interpolation is currently exercised.
*   Losses are evaluated offline.
*   They are not electrical power consumed by this switch (P-TC:
*   Conduction Losses / Switching Losses notes).
* vth_v = 1.88236969 (config/outputs/<vendor>/curve7_threshold_voltage.yaml)
* r_on_ohms = 0.0104446021 (Curve-3 rds_on at 10 V, conditions.Vgs_fixed; selection: nearest measured current point to i_load_a=10 A (runtime selection))
* vgs_on_v = 10 (config dpt.vgs_on; gate-drive metadata only)
* r_off_ohms = 1.90887435e+11 (source=measured_vgs0_dc_sweep; measured at Vgs=0 DC sweep as Roff=Vbus/Ioff; full provenance in source.r_off)
* vh_v = 0 (source=project_decision: zero hysteresis, switch tracks the Curve-7 threshold)
S_SW d s g s SW_T4
.MODEL SW_T4 SW(Ron=0.0104446021 Roff=1.90887435e+11 Vt=1.88236969 Vh=0)
* --- one measured linear output capacitor: solver stabilizer only ---
* coss_f = 4.53019131e-10 F (source=measured_curve4_capacitance; Curve-4 Coss at cap_ref_Vds; provenance in source.coss)
C_QOSS d s 4.53019131e-10

